#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "1. Introduction {#1-introduction}"
msgstr "1. Panimula {#1-introduction}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As a real time evolution technique, Trotterization consists in the "
"successive application of a quantum gate or gates, chosen to approximate the"
" time evolution of a system for a time slice. Following from the Schrödinger"
" equation, the time evolution of a system initially in the state "
"$\\vert\\psi(0)\\rangle$ takes the form:\n"
msgstr ""
"Bilang isang teknik para sa real-time na ebolusyon, ang Trotterization ay "
"binubuo ng sunud-sunod na aplikasyon ng isang quantum gate o mga gate, na "
"pinili upang mapalapitan ang ebolusyon ng sistema sa paglipas ng panahon "
"para sa isang time slice. Batay sa ekwasyon ng Schrödinger, ang ebolusyon ng"
" isang sistema na nagsimula sa estado $\\vert\\psi(0)\\rangle$ ay may "
"ganitong anyo:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi(t) \\rangle = e^{-i H t} \\vert \\psi(0) \\rangle \\text{,}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi(t) \\rangle = e^{-i H t} \\vert \\psi(0) \\rangle \\text{,}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where $H$ is the time-independent Hamiltonian governing the system. We "
"consider a Hamiltonian that can be written as a weighted sum of Pauli terms "
"$H=\\sum_j a_j P_j$, with $P_j$ representing a tensor product of Pauli terms"
" acting on $n$ qubits. In particular, these Pauli terms might commute with "
"one another, or they might not. Given a state at time $t=0$, how do we "
"obtain the system's state at a later time $|\\psi(t)\\rangle$ using a "
"quantum computer? The exponential of an operator can be most easily "
"understood through its Taylor series:\n"
msgstr ""
"kung saan ang $H$ ay ang time-independent na Hamiltonian na namamahala sa "
"sistema. Isinasaalang-alang natin ang isang Hamiltonian na maaaring isulat "
"bilang isang weighted sum ng mga Pauli term na $H=\\sum_j a_j P_j$, kung "
"saan ang $P_j$ ay kumakatawan sa tensor product ng mga Pauli term na "
"kumikilos sa $n$ qubits. Sa partikular, ang mga Pauli term na ito ay "
"maaaring mag-commute sa isa't isa, o hindi. Kapag ibinigay ang isang estado "
"sa oras na $t=0$, paano natin makukuha ang estado ng sistema sa susunod na "
"oras na $|\\psi(t)\\rangle$ gamit ang isang quantum computer? Ang "
"exponential ng isang operator ay pinakamadaling maunawaang sa pamamagitan ng"
" Taylor series nito:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"e^{-i H t} = 1-iHt-\\frac{1}{2}H^2t^2+...\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"e^{-i H t} = 1-iHt-\\frac{1}{2}H^2t^2+...\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Some very basic exponentials, like $e^{iZ}$ can be implemented easily on "
"quantum computers using a compact set of quantum gates. Most Hamiltonians of"
" interest will not have just a single term, but will instead have many "
"terms. Note what happens if $H = H_1+H_2$:\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang ilang napaka-simpleng exponential, tulad ng $e^{iZ}$, ay madaling "
"maipatupad sa mga quantum computer gamit ang isang maliit na hanay ng mga "
"quantum gate. Karamihan sa mga Hamiltonian na interesado tayo ay hindi "
"magkakaroon ng iisang term lamang, kundi maraming term. Pansinin kung ano "
"ang mangyayari kapag $H = H_1+H_2$:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"e^{-i H t} = 1-i(H_1+H_2)t-\\frac{1}{2}(H_1+H_2)^2t^2+...\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"e^{-i H t} = 1-i(H_1+H_2)t-\\frac{1}{2}(H_1+H_2)^2t^2+...\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When $H_1$ and $H_2$ commute, we have the familiar case (which is also true "
"for numbers, and variables $a$ and $b$ below):\n"
msgstr ""
"Kapag nag-commute ang $H_1$ at $H_2$, mayroon tayong pamilyar na kaso (na "
"totoo rin para sa mga numero, at sa mga variable na $a$ at $b$ sa ibaba):\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"e^{-i (a+b) t} = e^{-i a t}e^{-i b t}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"e^{-i (a+b) t} = e^{-i a t}e^{-i b t}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"But when operators do not commute, terms cannot be rearranged in the Taylor "
"series to simplify in this way. Thus, expressing complicated Hamiltonians in"
" quantum gates is a challenge.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ngunit kapag hindi nag-commute ang mga operator, ang mga term ay hindi "
"maaaring muling ayusin sa Taylor series upang ma-simplify sa ganitong "
"paraan. Kaya naman, ang pagpapahayag ng mga kumplikadong Hamiltonian sa mga "
"quantum gate ay isang hamon.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"One solution is to consider very small time $t$, such that the first-order "
"term in the Taylor expansion dominates. Under that assumption:\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang isang solusyon ay isaalang-alang ang napakaliit na oras na $t$, upang "
"ang first-order term sa Taylor expansion ang mangibabaw. Sa ilalim ng "
"pagpapalagay na iyon:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"e^{-i (H_1+H_2) t} \\approx 1-i(H_1+H_2)t \\approx (1-i H_1 t)(1-i H_2 t) \\approx e^{-i H_1 t}e^{-i H_2 t}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"e^{-i (H_1+H_2) t} \\approx 1-i(H_1+H_2)t \\approx (1-i H_1 t)(1-i H_2 t) \\approx e^{-i H_1 t}e^{-i H_2 t}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Of course, we might need to evolve our state for a longer time. That is "
"accomplished by using many such small steps in time. This process is called "
"Trotterization:\n"
msgstr ""
"Siyempre, maaaring kailangan nating paunlarin ang ating estado para sa mas "
"matagal na panahon. Ito ay nagagawa sa pamamagitan ng paggamit ng maraming "
"maliliit na hakbang sa oras. Ang prosesong ito ay tinatawag na "
"Trotterization:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi(t) \\rangle \\approx \\left(\\prod_j e^{-i a_j P_j t/r} \\right)^r \\vert\\psi(0) \\rangle \\text{,}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi(t) \\rangle \\approx \\left(\\prod_j e^{-i a_j P_j t/r} \\right)^r \\vert\\psi(0) \\rangle \\text{,}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here $t/r$ is the time slice (evolution step) that we are choosing. As a "
"result, a gate to be applied $r$ times is created. A smaller timestep leads "
"to a more accurate approximation. However, this also leads to deeper "
"circuits which, in practice, leads to more error accumulation (a non-"
"negligible concern on near-term quantum devices).\n"
msgstr ""
"Dito, ang $t/r$ ay ang time slice (evolution step) na pinipili natin. Bilang"
" resulta, isang gate ang nalilikha na ilalapat nang $r$ beses. Ang mas "
"maliit na timestep ay nagdudulot ng mas tumpak na pagpapalapita. Gayunpaman,"
" nagdudulot din ito ng mas malalim na circuits na, sa praktika, ay "
"nagdudulot ng mas maraming error accumulation (isang hindi mapapabayaang "
"alalahanin sa mga near-term na quantum device).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Today, we will study the time evolution of the [Ising "
"model](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ising_model) on linear lattices of "
"$N=2$ and $N=6$ sites. These lattices consist of an array of spins "
"$\\sigma_i$ that interact only with their nearest neighbors. These spins can"
" have two orientations: $\\uparrow$ and $\\downarrow$, which correspond to a"
" magnetization of $+1$ and $-1$ respectively.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa araw na ito, aaralin natin ang ebolusyon ng oras ng [Ising "
"model](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ising_model) sa mga linear na lattice "
"na may $N=2$ at $N=6$ na mga site. Ang mga lattice na ito ay binubuo ng "
"isang hanay ng mga spin na $\\sigma_i$ na nakikipag-ugnayan lamang sa "
"kanilang pinakamalapit na mga kapitbahay. Ang mga spin na ito ay maaaring "
"magkaroon ng dalawang oryentasyon: $\\uparrow$ at $\\downarrow$, na katumbas"
" ng magnetization na $+1$ at $-1$ ayon sa pagkakabanggit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"H = - J \\sum_{i=0}^{N-2} Z_i Z_{i+1} - h \\sum_{i=0}^{N-1} X_i  \\text{,}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"H = - J \\sum_{i=0}^{N-2} Z_i Z_{i+1} - h \\sum_{i=0}^{N-1} X_i  \\text{,}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where $J$ describes the interaction energy, and $h$ the magnitude of an "
"external field (in the x-direction above, but we will modify this). Let us "
"write this expression using Pauli matrices, and considering that the "
"external field has an angle $\\alpha$ with respect to the transversal "
"direction,\n"
msgstr ""
"kung saan ang $J$ ay naglalarawan ng interaction energy, at ang $h$ ang "
"magnitude ng isang panlabas na field (sa x-direksyon sa itaas, ngunit "
"babaguhin natin ito). Isulat natin ang ekspresyong ito gamit ang mga Pauli "
"matrix, at isaalang-alang na ang panlabas na field ay may anggulo na "
"$\\alpha$ kaugnay ng transversal na direksyon,\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"H = -J \\sum_{i=0}^{N-2} Z_i Z_{i+1} -h \\sum_{i=0}^{N-1} (\\sin\\alpha Z_i + \\cos\\alpha X_i) \\text{.}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"H = -J \\sum_{i=0}^{N-2} Z_i Z_{i+1} -h \\sum_{i=0}^{N-1} (\\sin\\alpha Z_i + \\cos\\alpha X_i) \\text{.}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This Hamiltonian is useful in that it allows us to easily study the effects "
"of an external field. In the computational basis, the system will be encoded"
" as follows:\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang Hamiltoniang ito ay kapaki-pakinabang dahil hinahayaan tayong madaling "
"pag-aralan ang mga epekto ng isang panlabas na field. Sa computational "
"basis, ang sistema ay ie-encode tulad ng sumusunod:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Quantum state            | Spin representation                        |\n"
"|:------------------------:|:------------------------------------------:|\n"
"| $\\lvert 0 0 0 0 \\rangle$ | $\\uparrow\\uparrow\\uparrow\\uparrow$         |\n"
"| $\\lvert 1 0 0 0 \\rangle$ | $\\downarrow\\uparrow\\uparrow\\uparrow$       |\n"
"| $\\ldots$                 | $\\ldots$                                   |\n"
"| $\\lvert 1 1 1 1 \\rangle$ | $\\downarrow\\downarrow\\downarrow\\downarrow$ |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Quantum state            | Representasyon ng Spin                     |\n"
"|:------------------------:|:------------------------------------------:|\n"
"| $\\lvert 0 0 0 0 \\rangle$ | $\\uparrow\\uparrow\\uparrow\\uparrow$         |\n"
"| $\\lvert 1 0 0 0 \\rangle$ | $\\downarrow\\uparrow\\uparrow\\uparrow$       |\n"
"| $\\ldots$                 | $\\ldots$                                   |\n"
"| $\\lvert 1 1 1 1 \\rangle$ | $\\downarrow\\downarrow\\downarrow\\downarrow$ |\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We will start investigating the time evolution of such a quantum system. "
"More specifically, we will visualize the time-evolution of certain "
"properties of the system like magnetization.\n"
msgstr ""
"Magsisimula tayong pag-aralan ang ebolusyon ng oras ng ganitong quantum "
"system. Mas partikular, i-visualize natin ang ebolusyon ng oras ng ilang "
"katangian ng sistema tulad ng magnetization.\n"

