#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"2.1 Defining the transverse-field Ising Hamiltonian {#21-defining-the-"
"transverse-field-ising-hamiltonian}"
msgstr ""
"2.1 Pagtukoy sa transverse-field Ising Hamiltonian {#21-defining-the-"
"transverse-field-ising-hamiltonian}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "We here consider the 1-D transverse-field Ising model.\n"
msgstr "Dito isinasaalang-alang natin ang 1-D transverse-field Ising model.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"First, we will create a function that takes in the system parameters $N$, "
"$J$, $h$ and $\\alpha$, and returns our Hamiltonian as a `SparsePauliOp`. A "
"[SparsePauliOp](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.SparsePauliOp)"
" is a sparse representation of an operator in terms of weighted "
"[Pauli](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.Pauli) "
"terms.\n"
msgstr ""
"Una, lilikha tayo ng isang function na tumatanggap ng mga parameter ng "
"sistema na $N$, $J$, $h$ at $\\alpha$, at nagbabalik ng ating Hamiltonian "
"bilang isang `SparsePauliOp`. Ang isang "
"[SparsePauliOp](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.SparsePauliOp)"
" ay isang sparse na representasyon ng isang operator sa mga tuntunin ng "
"weighted na mga "
"[Pauli](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.Pauli) "
"term.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Define the Hamiltonian {#define-the-hamiltonian}"
msgstr "Tukuyin ang Hamiltonian {#define-the-hamiltonian}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The system that we now consider has a size of $N=6$, $J=0.2$, $h=1.2$ and "
"$\\alpha=\\frac{\\pi}{8.0}$ as an example.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang sistema na isinasaalang-alang natin ngayon ay may sukat na $N=6$, "
"$J=0.2$, $h=1.2$ at $\\alpha=\\frac{\\pi}{8.0}$ bilang halimbawa.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"2.2 Set the parameters of the time-evolution simulation {#22-set-the-"
"parameters-of-the-time-evolution-simulation}"
msgstr ""
"2.2 Itakda ang mga parameter ng time-evolution simulation {#22-set-the-"
"parameters-of-the-time-evolution-simulation}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here we will consider three different Trotterization techniques:\n"
"* Lie–Trotter (first order)\n"
"* second-order Suzuki–Trotter\n"
"* fourth-order Suzuki–Trotter\n"
msgstr ""
"Dito isasaalang-alang natin ang tatlong iba't ibang teknik ng Trotterization:\n"
"* Lie–Trotter (first order)\n"
"* second-order Suzuki–Trotter\n"
"* fourth-order Suzuki–Trotter\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The latter two will be used in the exercise, and in the appendix.\n"
msgstr "Ang huli sa dalawa ay gagamitin sa ehersisyo, at sa appendix.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"2.3 Prepare the quantum circuit 1 (Initial state) {#23-prepare-the-quantum-"
"circuit-1-initial-state}"
msgstr ""
"2.3 Ihanda ang quantum circuit 1 (Paunang estado) {#23-prepare-the-quantum-"
"circuit-1-initial-state}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Create an initial state. Here we will start with a spin configuration of $\\uparrow\\uparrow\\downarrow\\downarrow\\uparrow\\uparrow$\n"
".\n"
msgstr ""
"Lumikha ng paunang estado. Dito magsisimula tayo sa isang spin configuration"
" na $\\uparrow\\uparrow\\downarrow\\downarrow\\uparrow\\uparrow$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-"
"quantum-computing/quantum-simulation/extracted-"
"outputs/b338806d-67bf-47ae-9d03-944bde3e2c99-0.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-"
"quantum-computing/quantum-simulation/extracted-"
"outputs/b338806d-67bf-47ae-9d03-944bde3e2c99-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"2.4 Prepare the quantum circuit 2 (Single circuit for time evolution) "
"{#24-prepare-the-quantum-circuit-2-single-circuit-for-time-evolution}"
msgstr ""
"2.4 Ihanda ang quantum circuit 2 (Iisang circuit para sa time evolution) "
"{#24-prepare-the-quantum-circuit-2-single-circuit-for-time-evolution}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "We here construct a circuit for a single time step using Lie–Trotter.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dito gumagawa tayo ng circuit para sa iisang time step gamit ang "
"Lie–Trotter.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The Lie product formula (first-order) is implemented in the "
"[LieTrotter](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.LieTrotter)"
" class. A first-order formula consists of the approximation stated in the "
"introduction, where the matrix exponential of a sum is approximated by a "
"product of matrix exponentials:\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang Lie product formula (first-order) ay ipinatupad sa klase na "
"[LieTrotter](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.LieTrotter)."
" Ang isang first-order formula ay binubuo ng pagpapalapita na binanggit sa "
"panimula, kung saan ang matrix exponential ng isang sum ay pinapalapitan ng "
"isang product ng mga matrix exponential:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"e^{H_1+H_2} \\approx e^{H_1} e^{H_2}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"e^{H_1+H_2} \\approx e^{H_1} e^{H_2}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As previously mentioned, very deep circuits lead to the accumulation of "
"errors, and cause problems for modern quantum computers. Because two-qubit "
"gates have higher error rates than single-qubit gates, a quantity of "
"particular interest is the two-qubit circuit depth. What really matters is "
"the two-qubit circuit depth after transpilation (since that is the circuit "
"the quantum computer actually executes). But let us get in the habit of "
"counting the operations for this circuit, even now using the simulator.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tulad ng nabanggit na, ang napakalalim na mga circuit ay nagdudulot ng "
"akumulasyon ng mga error, at nagdudulot ng mga problema para sa mga "
"modernong quantum computer. Dahil ang mga two-qubit gate ay may mas mataas "
"na rate ng error kaysa sa mga single-qubit gate, ang isang partikular na "
"interesadong dami ay ang two-qubit circuit depth. Ang talagang mahalaga ay "
"ang two-qubit circuit depth pagkatapos ng transpilation (dahil iyon ang "
"circuit na talagang isinasagawa ng quantum computer). Ngunit ugaliing "
"bilangin na natin ang mga operasyon para sa circuit na ito, kahit ngayon "
"gamit ang simulator.\n"

