#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We here show an example for constructing a circuit using higher-order (fourth-order) Suzuki–Trotter.\n"
"Now let's try constructing a circuit simulation with fourth-order Suzuki–Trotter following the examples shown above.\n"
msgstr ""
"Nagpapakita tayo rito ng isang halimbawa ng pagbuo ng circuit gamit ang mas mataas na order na (ikaapat na order) Suzuki–Trotter.\n"
"Subukan nating bumuo ng circuit simulation gamit ang ikaapat na order na Suzuki–Trotter ayon sa mga halimbawang ipinakita sa itaas.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The fourth-order Suzuki–Trotter can be used in Qiskit by means of the "
"[SuzukiTrotter "
"class](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.SuzukiTrotter)."
" The fourth-order can be evaluated using the following recursion relation. "
"Note that the order of Suzuki–Trotter is denoted as \"2k\" in the following "
"equations.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang ikaapat na order na Suzuki–Trotter ay maaaring gamitin sa Qiskit sa "
"pamamagitan ng [SuzukiTrotter "
"class](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.SuzukiTrotter)."
" Ang ikaapat na order ay maaaring kalkulahin gamit ang sumusunod na "
"recursion relation. Tandaan na ang order ng Suzuki–Trotter ay tinutukoy "
"bilang \"2k\" sa mga sumusunod na equation.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{U}_{ST(2k)}\\left(t\\right) = \\left[ \\hat{U}_{ST(2k-2)}\\left(p_k t\\right) \\right]^2 \\hat{U}_{ST(2k-2)}\\left( (1- 4 p_k) t\\right)\\left[ \\hat{U}_{ST(2k-2)}\\left(p_k t\\right) \\right]^2\n"
"$$\n"
"$$\n"
"p_k = 1 / \\left(4-4^{\\frac{1}{2k-1}}\\right)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{U}_{ST(2k)}\\left(t\\right) = \\left[ \\hat{U}_{ST(2k-2)}\\left(p_k t\\right) \\right]^2 \\hat{U}_{ST(2k-2)}\\left( (1- 4 p_k) t\\right)\\left[ \\hat{U}_{ST(2k-2)}\\left(p_k t\\right) \\right]^2\n"
"$$\n"
"$$\n"
"p_k = 1 / \\left(4-4^{\\frac{1}{2k-1}}\\right)\n"
"$$\n"

